title: Prices Are Rising Again
subtitle: Workers are seeing their purchasing power decline.
view-if: inflation >= 5 and high_inflation_timer = 0 and spd_in_government
new-page: true
on-arrival: capital_strike_progress += 1; workers_spd -= 4; old_middle_spd -= 5; new_middle_spd -= 5; rural_spd -= 4; unemployed_spd -= 4; pensioners_spd -= 3; high_inflation_timer = 6; high_inflation_timer = 4 if inflation > 6; high_inflation_timer = 2 if inflation >= 8; trust_in_democracy -= 4; old_middle_afd += 2; new_middle_afd += 2; rural_afd += 2
tags: event

= Prices Are Rising Again

Inflation is up again. Rent, food and energy bills are eating into everyone's income, and the memory of the 2022 energy shock is still fresh. The tabloids print shopping-basket comparisons every week.

People and press are demanding that the government act.

- @taxes: Raise taxes to cool the economy.
- @welfare: Cut government spending.
- @price_controls: Cap energy and rent prices.
- @bank: Surely the European Central Bank will act?
- @nothing: Realistically, there is nothing we can do.

@taxes
on-arrival: upper_tax_rates += 1; lower_tax_rates += 1; budget += 2; unemployment_rate += 0.4; capital_strike_progress -= 1; inflation -= 0.8; new_middle_spd -= 3; old_middle_spd -= 3; workers_spd -= 3; rural_spd -= 3; linke_coalition_dissent += 1; linke_relation -= 5; left_dissent += 5; economic_growth -= 0.3

Raising taxes is unpopular with everyone, but it may be what it takes to bring inflation under control.

@welfare
on-arrival: welfare -= 1; budget += 1; capital_strike_progress -= 2; unemployment_rate += 0.4; new_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 4*(1-dissent); workers_spd -= 5; unemployed_spd -= 5; inflation -= 0.8; left_dissent += 5; labor_dissent += 5; center_dissent += 5; linke_coalition_dissent += 1; economic_growth -= 0.3

Spending less should cool the economy, according to the textbooks. But the pain falls on the people who are already struggling the most.

@price_controls
on-arrival: capital_strike_progress += 3; inflation -= 1.5; coalition_dissent += 1; unemployment_rate += 0.2; old_middle_spd -= 4; new_middle_spd -= 2; rural_spd -= 3; workers_spd += 2; unemployed_spd += 3; fdp_relation -= 6; cdu_relation -= 4; greens_relation -= 2; economic_growth -= 0.2; budget -= 1

An energy price cap and a national rent freeze are popular with tenants and workers, but landlords, energy companies and the liberal press are furious. Inflation does fall, at least for now.

@bank
on-arrival: capital_strike_progress += 1; inflation -= 0.3

The ECB raises interest rates again. That will bring inflation down in time, but it also makes mortgages and investment more expensive, and the ECB reminds Berlin that fiscal policy is the government's job.

@nothing
on-arrival: capital_strike_progress += 1

Realistically, there is nothing we can do to stop the rise in prices.
